From 24b356795ff76d5be08d4b7be44b2c86f67f9aff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(chunks): restore the lighting and scheduling foundation

Retain computed chunk lighting, nearest-first request scheduling and complete-column sends after upstream reverted their implementation. The connected-shape, incremental-lighting and subchunk-response patches depend on these caches and queues. Later patches add bounded jobs, compact snapshots, native light filtering and regression coverage.

Restore the upstream foundation as an explicit prerequisite while preserving the new upstream palette validation, block-state upgrade data and chunk-loading fixes.
